==English==

===Alternative spellings===
* [[ostler]]

===Etymology===
Syncopated form of {{term|hosteler}} < {{etyl|frm}} {{term|hostiler}} < {{etyl|fro}} {{term|hostelier}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|hostilarius|lang=la}} < {{term|hospitalarius|lang=la}} < {{term|hospitale|lang=la}} "inn" < {{term|hospitalis|hospitālis|lang=la}} "hospitable" < {{term|hospes|lang=la}} "host, guest".  Both hostler and its alternate form "[[ostler]]" originally meant simply "inkeeper", and acquired a specific association with horses in the second half of the 14th century.

